sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: One data question — the journey in time order
    accDescr: A typical successful data question moves between the browser, app, AI provider, and database. SQL is drafted and checked before read-only execution. The app can explain all loaded rows (up to 1,000) before returning the final answer and table. Direct answers and failures are covered in the assistant and cancellation diagrams.
    autonumber
    actor B as Your browser
    participant APP as App server
    participant AI as AI provider
    participant DB as Database

    B->>APP: Ask a question with recent context
    APP->>AI: Use the question and table list
    AI-->>APP: Draft a SQL query
    APP-->>B: Show progress and SQL preview
    APP->>APP: Check that the query is allowed
    APP->>DB: Run the checked read-only query
    DB-->>APP: Return up to 1,000 rows
    opt Explain the results
        APP->>AI: Explain all loaded rows (up to 1,000)
        AI-->>APP: Result explanation
    end
    APP-->>B: Final answer, table, and any warnings
